WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.061
Meet Osteon, your anatomy and physiology
study space.

2
00:00:04.664 --> 00:00:06.955
Drag to rotate. Scroll to zoom.

3
00:00:06.955 --> 00:00:10.215
Double-click a bone to explore its region;

4
00:00:10.215 --> 00:00:13.298
double-click again to focus on that bone.

5
00:00:13.298 --> 00:00:14.708
Use Back to return.

6
00:00:15.393 --> 00:00:18.793
Switch between the axial and appendicular
skeletons.

7
00:00:19.393 --> 00:00:22.304
Turn regional colors on to compare
neighboring bones.

8
00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:24.456
Here is the foramen magnum:

9
00:00:25.056 --> 00:00:27.279
the large opening in the occipital bone.

10
00:00:28.034 --> 00:00:30.968
Hide the label, then test yourself with a
numbered target

11
00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:32.056
and check your answer.

12
00:00:32.588 --> 00:00:36.877
Need a nudge? Open the Socratic tutor and
choose an installed

13
00:00:36.877 --> 00:00:40.165
Ollama model. Ask for one question at a
time.

14
00:00:40.699 --> 00:00:43.965
It uses your current study context and
links to the supplied

15
00:00:43.965 --> 00:00:44.943
textbook readings.

16
00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:49.452
Then connect what you see with OpenStax
chapters six and

17
00:00:49.452 --> 00:00:50.963
seven in the study studio.

18
00:00:51.569 --> 00:00:55.791
Explore, identify, and return to what
needs practice, on

19
00:00:55.791 --> 00:00:59.902
desktop or phone. Try Osteon free in your
browser.

20
00:01:00.769 --> 00:01:04.325
No account needed. Local tutoring requires
Ollama.
